# condor_submit_dag sweep_45_dumusque_mu.dag : sweep_4096.dag and sweep_fraction.dag (45 s magnetograms) again with the
# bisector of Dumusque (2014) times mu added to the spots (settings_45_dumusque_mu.sh: convective_shift = 1,
# dumusque_mu_scaling = 0, 1), both kinds of faculae, everything in ${BASE}/dumusque_mu. The identification and the
# filling factors are those of sweep_4096.dag and sweep_fraction.dag (they do not depend on the bisector): run it after
# both have done their aggregate step.
#   1. the grids once per T_sp of the two parameter files, with the new bisector (build_grids_45_dumusque_mu.sub)
#   2. one simulation per line of the parameter files (run_opt_rv_45_dumusque_mu_plage.sub, ..._fraction.sub)
#   3. table of all the sets and the figures, per kind (collect_stats_45_dumusque_mu.sub; it runs even if some sets failed)
JOB grids             build_grids_45_dumusque_mu.sub
JOB sets_plage        run_opt_rv_45_dumusque_mu_plage.sub
JOB sets_fraction     run_opt_rv_45_dumusque_mu_fraction.sub
JOB collect_plage     collect_stats_45_dumusque_mu.sub
JOB collect_fraction  collect_stats_45_dumusque_mu.sub
VARS collect_plage      kind="plage"
VARS collect_fraction   kind="fraction"
PARENT grids CHILD sets_plage sets_fraction
PARENT sets_plage CHILD collect_plage
PARENT sets_fraction CHILD collect_fraction
SCRIPT POST sets_plage     /bin/true
SCRIPT POST sets_fraction  /bin/true
